# text = I have no doubt that we shall have some monster of the middle class , some tinker or tailor , or candlestick-maker , with his long purse , preaching reform and practising corruption : exactly as the liberals did under Walpole : bribery was unknown in the time of the Stuarts ; but we have a capital registration , Mr Tadpole tells me .
