# text = And you -- shall I bring you a glass of nature's wine I have drank of the spring of the Holy Abbey and none other must touch my lips this eve Come , our course must be brisk I hope that if ever we regain our right , my father , and that we ever can save by the interposition of divine will seems to me clearly impossible , that you will never forget how bitter it is to he driven from the soil ; and that you will bring back the people to the land I would pursue our right for no other cause After centuries of sorrow and degradation , it should never be said , that we had no sympathy with the sad and the oppressed After centuries of sorrow and degradation let it not be said that you acquired your right only to create a baron or a squire Nay , thou shalt have thy way , Stephen if ever the good hour come .
